Subject: [PATCH 24/27] Compare in pieces (VICTORY_COMPARE_PIECES=1, off):
 refreshes' compare buffer capped at 1 MiB

A refresh with VICTORY_COPY_CHANGED read the title's range into a
thread's buffer as large as the range (up to 16 MiB) and compared it
whole; each of the 12 refreshing threads kept a buffer as large as the
largest range it ever compared (the heap profile: ~270 MB live in the
first area). With the switch the range is read and compared 1 MiB at a
time through one 1 MiB buffer, and the spans of the pieces are joined as
one compare of the whole joins them (a test checks them against the
whole, across the pieces' edges). The bytes copied and the runs sent are
those of before.
